setslot('da',70,41,'Men for at Cato alene kunne give eksempler på enhver dyd, ser det ud til, at hans gode skæbne sørgede for, at han havde ondt i den hånd, han gav sig selv stødet med. Så fik han tid til at se døden i øjnene og kæmpe med den, og hans mod voksede i faren i stedet for at svækkes. Hvis det havde været min opgave at fremstille ham i hans stolteste øjeblik, ville jeg have vist ham gennemblødt af blod, mens han rev sine indvolde ud, snarere end med sværdet i hånden, som hans tids billedhuggere gjorde. For dette andet drab på ham selv var langt voldsommere end det første.')
setslot('en',70,41,'But so that Cato alone might supply examples of every virtue, it seems that his good destiny made his hand hurt when he struck himself. This gave him time to face death and grapple with it, strengthening his courage in danger instead of weakening it. Had I been the one to portray him at his proudest moment, I would have shown him drenched in blood, tearing out his entrails, rather than with a sword in his hand, as the sculptors of his time did. For this second killing of himself was far more violent than the first.')
